# Docker build context for BOTH the server and dashboard images is the repo
# root (see docker-compose.yml's `server.build`/`dashboard.build` and
# server/Dockerfile / dashboard/Dockerfile) — needed so each Dockerfile can
# COPY the root pnpm-lock.yaml/pnpm-workspace.yaml for a workspace-aware,
# frozen-lockfile install of just that one package. Everything below is
# either irrelevant to both images or something that should never be baked
# into a layer. Neither Dockerfile does a blanket `COPY . .`, so this file is
# a context-size/leak-prevention measure, not a correctness requirement —
# but it must NOT exclude `server/` or `dashboard/` themselves, since each
# image's Dockerfile COPYs its own workspace member from this same context.

# Never bake real secrets into an image layer.
.env
.env.*

node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo
server/test

.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.log
coverage
**/coverage
docs
*.md
.atl
